cus is lost in modals, several controls are unreachable, and focus indicators are inconsistent.\" One remediation pass over the four flows. One epic.\n\nBut wait — could split by flow? No — same component/team, one logical change.\n\nSo plan:\n- E001: Dashboard keyboard accessibility fixes (HLR-1, HLR-2), P1, component Dashboard, Implementation.\n- E002: Documentation — VPAT and accessibility statement update (HLR-3), P2, implementation_type=docs-authoring, blocked by E001 (Rule 11: docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics). Priority: docs-authoring exception — strategy frontmatter priority Normal → P2. Good, matches HLR-3 P2.\n\nStep 5 DAG: E001 → E002.\n\nRule 24: docs-authoring epic gets \"technically reviewed against implementation\" AC. HLR-3 already says \"with technical review.\"\n\nComponents: need canonical names. Check .context/rhai-components.txt. Also architecture context for Dashboard and Documentation to score signal 9.\n\nTeam: strategy doesn't specify teams. Affected Components has no owner teams. I need to infer — maybe use a generic team like \"Dashboard\" team? Let me check rhai-components.txt and architecture context, which may list owner teams. Let me look at the eval context — maybe there's a convention from other cases. Let me explore the workspace.\n\nHealth warnings: missing Impacted Teams table, Dependencies table, Acceptance Criteria (no Given/When/Then), NFR section. Note them.\n\nAC derivation: strategy has no Given/When/Then ACs; derive from HLRs — e.g., each of the four flows completable by keyboard alone in automated/DOM-level checks, no focus traps, focus visible on all interactive controls.\n\nLet me check the .context files.","signature":"4e7a9a1cd1cb428a8ff8f72303823cb4"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":18665,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3258536ce2e6f27","agent_id":"adc00a8c258f6d0a3","session_id":"5d78f5