 by\n  keyboard traversal and operable by keyboard activation.\n- No focus traps remain in the audited flows: focus can always leave modals\n  and dialogs, and focus returns to the invoking element when they close.\n- Focus is visibly indicated on all interactive controls in the audited flows,\n  with one consistent indicator style across all four flows.\n- Every defect enumerated in the audit report for the four flows is verified\n  fixed, with the verification recorded per defect.\n- The functional behavior of the four flows is unchanged apart from the\n  accessibility remediation (no regressions introduced).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)** — the four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard,\n  with no focus traps or unreachable controls: covered by this epic.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)** — visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited\n  flows: covered by this epic. Bundled with HLR-1 rather than split: both HLRs\n  are remediated in a single pass over the same four flows in the same\n  component and team — the audit's defect list interleaves focus traps,\n  unreachable controls, and inconsistent indicators per flow, so a split would\n  force two passes over the same UI surfaces and add an artificial\n  serialization edge between epics building the same surface.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26897,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3258536ce2e6f27","agent_id":"adc00a8c258f6d0a3","session_id":"5d78f521-7e82-4c71-8bdb-ec850ccb8e22","uuid":"f6abef62-3c0b-4e86-ac5e-ccee62dac5ec","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:20:20.740Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9017"}
