{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aad382e9f652ea1c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9017\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: Epic Boundaries\n9\t  description: E001 is a single sweep over four enumerated flows that sits at the\n10\t    ~2-week line; Health Warnings carry no conditional re-split trigger for it. Record\n11\t    a concrete re-split trigger in Health Warnings, e.g. split along flow boundaries\n12\t    if per-flow remediation exceeds a set day budget.\n13\terror: null\n14\t---\n15\t# Decomposition Review — RHAISTRAT-9017\n16\t\n17\t## Review Summary\n18\t\n19\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n20\tRecommendation: accept\n21\t\n22\tContract validator: OK (`validate_decomposition.py` exited 0 — body sections,\n23\tcanonical component names, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, priority inheritance, and\n24\timplementation-type parallelism all pass). Triage consistency: `triage: null`\n25\twith `epic_count: 2` — full decomposition, multi-epic output expected, no\n26\tcontradiction.\n27\t\n28\t## Criterion Details\n29\t\n30\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n31\tAll three HLRs map to epics: HLR-1 and HLR-2 → E001, HLR-3 → E002. The\n32\tHLR-2 bundling into E001 is correct under the shared-surface rule — both HLRs\n33\tare remediated in one pass over the same four flows, same component, same\n34\tteam — and the coupling rationale is recorded inline in the HLR Traceability\n35\tMatrix row (and repeated in the epic's HLR Traceability section), satisfying\n36\tthe bundling-recording requirement. No priority collapse: HLR-3 is a genuinely\n37\tdistinct deferrable work stream (Documentation component, separate review\n38\tcycle) and correctly sits in its own epic. Priority inheritance: E001 (P1)\n39\tblocks only E002 (P2), and E002 is a docs-authoring epic whose P2 derives\n40\tfrom the strategy's `priority: Normal` per the docs-authoring exempti