{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8465a431b2bc3c14","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9017-E001\n3\ttitle: Keyboard accessibility remediation for core Dashboard flows\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9017\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Keyboard accessibility remediation for core Dashboard flows\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic remediates the keyboard-accessibility defects that the accessibility\n34\taudit enumerated in the four core Dashboard flows — project creation, workbench\n35\tspawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission. The audit found that focus\n36\tis lost in modals, several controls are unreachable by keyboard, and focus\n37\tindicators are inconsistent. This epic delivers all four flows fully operable\n38\tby keyboard alone, with no focus traps, no unreachable controls, and consistent\n39\tvisible focus indication.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Remediate every keyboard-operability defect the audit enumerated in the four\n44\t  audited flows: focus loss and focus traps in modals and dialogs, and controls\n45\t  that cannot be reached or activated with keyboard input.\n46\t- Apply a consistent, visible focus indicator to all interactive controls\n47\t  across the four audited flows, replacing the inconsistent indicator styles\n48\t  the audit found.\n49\t- Include screen-reader semantics only where the keyboard fixes require them;\n50\t  broader screen-reader work is out of scope.\n51\t- Flows outside the four audited ones are out of scope.\n52\t- Verification of the fixes per flow (keyboard walkthrough or scripted\n53\t  keyboard-traversal checks against the audit's defect list).\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Each of the four audited flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model\n58\t  deployment, pipeline run submission) can be completed end-to-end using\n59\t  keyboard input alone, with no step that requires a pointing device.\n60\t- Every interactive control exposed in the audited flows is reachable by\n61\t  keyboard traversal and operable by keyboard activation.\n62\t- No focus traps remain in the audited flows: focus can always leave modals\n63\t  and dialogs, and focus returns to the invoking element when they close.\n64\t- Focus is visibly indicated on all interactive controls in the audited flows,\n65\t  with one consistent indicator style across all four flows.\n66\t- Every defect enumerated in the audit report for the four flows is verified\n67\t  fixed, with the verification recorded per defect.\n68\t- The functional behavior of the four flows is unchanged apart from the\n69\t  accessibility remediation (no regressions introduced).\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- **HLR-1 (P1)** — the four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard,\n74\t  with no focus traps or unreachable controls: covered by this epic.\n75\t- **HLR-2 (P1)** — visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited\n76\t  flows: covered by this epic. Bundled with HLR-1 rather than split: both HLRs\n77\t  are remediated in a single pass over the same four flows in the same\n78\t  component and team — the audit's defect list interleaves focus traps,\n79\t  unreachable controls, and inconsistent indicators per flow, so a split would\n80\t  force two passes over the same UI surfaces and add an artificial\n81\t  serialization edge between epics building the same surface.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-887b2e358a0d4f85","agent_id":"a6e150e2033ee2355","session_id":"5d78f521-7e82-4c71-8bdb-ec850ccb8e22","uuid":"0f753e47-f69a-472f-89b5-7c6d002035cc","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:26:16.477Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8465a431b2bc3c14","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
